{
  "company_name": "RestorePower Gen",
  "industry": "Power Generation",
  "use_case": "Generator outage response and restoration tracking",
  "space_title": "RestorePower Gen - Outage Response & Restoration 🔌",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Power Generation\n\n**Use case:** Generator Outage Response & Restoration\n\nRestorePower Gen — outage management and restoration analytics across 20 generating units (gas turbine, combined cycle, steam, diesel, hydro). Plant Managers and Reliability Engineers use this space to track EFOR, MTTR, and forced-outage cause codes; the Fleet Performance team and CFO use it to quantify lost-generation revenue, rank repair-cost outliers, and prioritize capex on chronic offenders.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Equivalent Forced Outage Rate (EFOR) — NERC GADS benchmark; fleet target <5%\n- Equivalent Availability Factor (EAF) — industry target >90%\n- Mean Time To Repair (MTTR) hours — restoration efficiency\n- Forced outage count — reliability of unplanned downtime\n- Lost generation (MWh) — revenue exposure from outages\n- Repair cost ($) — maintenance budget driver\n- Parts on hand (%) — supply-chain readiness for restoration\n- Restoration progress (%) — active-event tracking\n\n**Data sources**\n- `generating_units` — daily runtime, availability, output, operational status per unit\n- `outage_events` — outage records with cause code, duration, lost generation, repair cost\n- `repair_snapshots` — weekly repair progress, crew deployment, parts, restoration ETA",
