  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports outage response and restoration tracking for a 20-unit fleet (gas turbine, combined cycle, steam, diesel, hydro). Personas: Plant Manager (operational_status, availability_pct, repair progress), Reliability Engineer (cause_code, forced outage trends, MTTR), Fleet Performance (EFOR, EAF), and CFO (lost_generation_mwh revenue impact, repair_cost_usd).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Availability = availability_pct; fleet target >90%, with EAF >88% considered healthy per NERC GADS.\n- EFOR (Equivalent Forced Outage Rate) = forced_outage_count divided by service hours; target <5% for thermal, <8% for peakers.\n- MTTR = avg_outage_duration_hours on outage_events; goal varies by cause: mechanical ~48h, electrical ~24h.\n- Lost generation = lost_generation_mwh; multiply by ~$45/MWh for revenue-impact estimate.\n- Repair cost = repair_cost_usd; outliers > $100K should trigger root-cause review.\n- Parts readiness = parts_on_hand_pct; <80% is a restoration risk.\n- Forced vs Planned outage ratio — forced/(forced+planned); target <30%.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - outage_kpi_monthly (source: outage_events) — dims: outage_date, unit_type, outage_type, cause_code; measures: total_outage_events, total_lost_generation_mwh, avg_outage_duration_hours, total_repair_cost, forced_outage_count, unique_unit_count, max_duration_hours.\n  - unit_availability_monthly (source: generating_units) — dims: record_date, unit_type, station, operational_status; measures: avg_availability_pct, total_output_mwh, total_runtime_hours, running_unit_count, total_unit_count, max_runtime_hours.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. unit_id, unit_name, parts_on_hand_pct, restoration_progress_pct, cost_to_date_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly forced outage count by unit type for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 units by total lost generation MWh year-to-date.",
    "Which cause codes drive the most repair cost this year, and what is the average duration?",
    "How has fleet average availability trended month-over-month, broken out by station?",
    "Which units have an active repair with parts on hand below 80% and restoration progress below 50%?",
    "Top 10 outages by repair cost USD in the last 90 days — and how does that compare to the prior 90?",
    "What is the monthly trend in average outage duration hours (MTTR) for forced outages?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique units?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT outage_date, MEASURE(unique_unit_count) AS unique_unit_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.outage_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY outage_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest duration hours changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT outage_date, MEASURE(max_duration_hours) AS max_duration_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.outage_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY outage_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest runtime hours?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, MEASURE(max_runtime_hours) AS max_runtime_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.unit_availability_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has running unit count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, MEASURE(running_unit_count) AS running_unit_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.unit_availability_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does total hours of operation in the day break down by generator unit identifier for 'Forced Outage' records?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT unit_id, COUNT(*) AS record_count, SUM(runtime_hours) AS total_runtime_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.generating_units",
        "WHERE operational_status = 'Forced Outage' GROUP BY unit_id ORDER BY total_runtime_hours DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total repair and restoration cost in usd over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT outage_date, SUM(repair_cost_usd) AS total_repair_cost_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.outage_events",
        "GROUP BY outage_date ORDER BY outage_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average percentage of required parts available changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, AVG(parts_on_hand_pct) AS avg_parts_on_hand_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.repair_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sql_snippets": {
